splice-test: count the bytes a pipe read returned, not the bytes asked for

read_from_pipe() subtracts the requested size from the remaining count, so
a short pipe read (any read of a 76800-byte buffer from a 64 KiB pipe) makes
the reader believe it consumed more than it did; it exits early and the
writer's next splice gets EPIPE unless it wins the race. A kernel page-cache
splice usually wins; a FUSE O_DIRECT splice (one daemon round trip) usually
loses, so generic/591 failed on FrankenFS for the test program's reason, not
the filesystem's (bd-hryzs).

--- a/src/splice-test.c
+++ b/src/splice-test.c
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 			fprintf(stderr, "read: %s: unexpected EOF\n", filename);
 			exit(1);
 		}
-		size -= sz;
+		size -= ret;
 	}
 	free(buffer);
 }
